          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            5.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#ExceptionalIsomorphism Exceptional isomorphism
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
            %p
              There is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+isomorphism"} exceptional isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Spin(5)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    Sp(2)
            %p
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%285%29"} Spin(5)
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+unitary+group"} quaternionic unitary group
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℍ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(2) = U(2,\mathbb{H})
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
            %p
              This is an indirect consequence of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triality"} triality
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#CadekVanzura97"} Čadek-Vanžura 97
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              be a 4-dimensional complex vector space with an inner product and a compatible complex volume form. As explained
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Spin%286%29#ExceptionalIsomorphism"} here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mn 2
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^2 V
              whose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1
              eigenspaces, say
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mo ±
                        %mn 2
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_{\pm}^2 V
              %em real
              inner product spaces. Thus, the group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{SU}(V)
              acts as linear transformations of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mo ±
                      %mn 2
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_{\pm}^2 V
              that preserve the inner product, giving a homomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SU
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mo ±
                        %mn 2
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho: \mathrm{SU}(V) \to \mathrm{O}(\Lambda_{\pm}^2 V)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{SU}(V)
              in a 2-1 and onto way to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SO
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mo ±
                        %mn 2
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{SO}(\Lambda_{\pm}^2 V)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = \mathbb{C}^4
              this shows
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SU
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 6
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{SU}(4) \cong \mathrm{Spin}(6)
            %p
              Now suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is additionally equipped with an complex symplectic structure, i.e. a nondegenerate skew-symmetric complex-bilinear form
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mn 2
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \in \Lambda^2 V
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sp}(V)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{SU}(V)
              preserving this extra structure is isomorphic to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+symplectic+group"} compact symplectic group
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sp}(2)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+unitary+group"} quaternionic unitary group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sp}(V)
              acts on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_+^2 V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_-^2 V
              preserving
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mn 2
                      %mi V
                      %mo =
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⊕
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mo −
                        %mn 2
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \in \Lambda^2 V = \Lambda_+^2 V \oplus \Lambda_-^2 V
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sp}(V)
              is compact, every invariant subspace has an invariant complement, so one or both of the 6-dimensional subspaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_+^2 V
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mo −
                      %mn 2
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_-^2 V
              must have a 5-dimensional subspace invariant under the action of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sp}(V)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo :
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 6
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho: \mathrm{SU}(4) \to \mathrm{SO}(6)
              restricts to a 2-1 homomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SO
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 5
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma : \mathrm{Sp}(2) \to \mathrm{SO}(5)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 10
                    %mo =
                    %mi dim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \dim(\mathrm{Sp}(2)) = 10 = \dim(\mathrm{SO}(5))
            %p
              the differential
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\sigma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo :
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma : \mathrm{Sp}(2) \to \mathrm{SO}(5)
              is actually a double cover. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sp}(2)
              is connected this implies
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 5
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sp}(2) \cong \mathrm{Spin}(5)
          %p
